BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ruby Gill + Mimi Gilbert (Poetry)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260315T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260315T230000
DTSTAMP:20260315T133137
UID:ganggang-10001226-1773597600-1773615600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/02/Screenshot-2026-02-02-at-12.01.20-pm.png
CREATED:20260202T010428Z
DESCRIPTION:Don’t miss Mimi Gilbert (USA) and Ruby Gill (Australia /
  South Africa) and as they embark on a once-in-a-lifetime\, intimate tour 
 of Australia this autumn\, bringing their award-winning alt-folk and profo
 und poetry to an exciting series of shows in big and small places near you
 . The two opinionated\, light-hearted\, torch-carriers of language have b
 een fast friends for many years\, and will be reuniting for an intimate to
 ur across Australia this March and April. For Mimi Gilbert\, this is a lau
 nch tour for their new record ‘Undrowning\,’ a record made between C
 alifornia and Australia. In support\, Ruby will be performing a new\, neve
 r-before-seen set of mostly spoken-word poetry (and a few songs)\, celebra
 ting the release of their new poetry book ‘I’m not exaggerating when 
 I say’.  \n\n\n\nThis experience is bound to be unforgettable – each 
 artist will bring their own flawless minimalism and unforgettable lyrical 
 honesty to the table\, with protest songs\, witnessing of nature\, explora
 tion of queerness and deep love for family and politics that are beloved b
 y audiences all over the globe. Both will leave you a little changed from 
 when you walked in the door. \n\n\n\nMore about Mimi Gilbert  \n\n\n\nMim
 i Gilbert is an independent artist who has spent the better part of the la
 st 10 years living\, touring and creating music in the USA\, Australia and
  New Zealand. Previously based in Melbourne now back in Ojai/ Los Angeles\
 , the Californian born has toured most recently with Julia Jacklin and Ang
 ie McMahon. Mimi shares a deeply-crafted\, folk-inflected approach to thei
 r songwriting. \n\n\n\nPronounced ‘the best kept secret in the music ind
 ustry’ by Double J – Australia\, Mimi established themself as a talent
 ed singer and guitarist capable of ruminative insight and quietly devastat
 ing song-craft\, inviting comparisons to Laura Marling and Big Thief’s A
 drianne Lenker. The album left deep ripples among many\, picking up accola
 des such as Double J and FBi Radio Feature album and noted by NME as one o
 f their ‘Top 10 album picks’. \n\n\n\nMore about Ruby Gill  \n\n\n\nR
 uby Gill was born and raised in South Africa\, now based in regional VIC\,
  and has spent the last 9 years bringing even the most stoic global audien
 ces to tears with her effortless musicality and powerful poetry. Ruby was 
 recently shortlisted for the Australian Music Prize (top 3 in the country)
  for her ARIA-charting\, globally renowned record ‘Some Kind Of Control\
 ,’ and has toured with the likes of Missy Higgins\, Bongeziwe Mabandla\,
  Nakhane\, Mon Rovia (Liberia)\, Stella Donnelly\, Angie McMahon and more\
 , with Port Fairy Folk Festival’s Emerging Artist of the Year award\, Mu
 sic Victoria’s Best Folk Work nomination\, and The Times’ Breaking Act
  accolade to her name among others. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed
  to an inclusive and safe experience for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair
  accessible with accessible restrooms. We have zero tolerance for harassme
 nt and have support measures in place to ensure everyone’s safety. For s
 pecific accessibility needs or assistance\, please contact us in advance. 
 We aim to make our events enjoyable for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe a
 cknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people\, the Traditional Custodians 
 of the land where our events take place. We pay our respects to their Elde
 rs past\, present\, and emerging\, and recognise their enduring connection
  to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are grateful to celebrate music a
 nd dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T010429Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/ruby-gill-mimi-gilbert-poetry/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ranagri (Ireland/England) at Gang Gang
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260318T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260318T213000
DTSTAMP:20260315T133137
UID:ganggang-10001236-1773858600-1773869400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/02/Screenshot-2026-02-25-at-9.40.16-am.png
CREATED:20260224T224123Z
DESCRIPTION:Peace Run Records is proud to present Ranagri (England) at Gan
 g Gang Cafe on Wednesday 11 March. With doors at 6.30pm and show start 7pm
 \, tickets are $35 entry presale and $40 on the door. Ranagri are coming o
 ut to Australia for the first time and we are so excited to be bringing th
 is incredible contemporary folk band to Canberra as a Blue Mountains Music
  Festival sideshow. Supported by Australian/Fijian Folk-soul singer Andrea
  Kirwin\, this concert will feature a variety of instruments including cig
 ar box guitar\, acoustic guitar\, flute\, harp\, percussion and more. \n\n
 \n\nRanagri is an award winning folk band from Ireland and England. With a
  unique blend of instruments that includes voices\, guitar\, bouzouki\, fl
 utes\, whistles\, harp/electric harp\, and bodhrán/drums\, they create a 
 sound that is both mesmerising and unforgettable. \n\n\n\nThe band has rec
 orded five studio albums to date\, with their latest release\, ‘Traditio
 n II\,’ receiving critical acclaim upon its release in July 2022. Folk R
 adio UK placed the album in their top 10 albums of 2022\, cementing the ba
 nd’s status as one of the most exciting and innovative folk bands in the
  UK today. \n\n\n\nPrevious critically acclaimed albums\, ‘Playing For L
 uck\,’ ‘Fort of the Hare\,’ and ‘The Great Irish Songbook’ (with
  pop legend Tony Christie)\, were recorded at the Grammy Award- winning St
 ockfisch Records label. The band’s third album\, ‘VOICES\,’ was reco
 rded at Peter Gabriel’s Real World Studios and along with the album ‘T
 radition’ were both released on GoatsKin Records. \n\n\n\nRanagri has es
 tablished themselves as a standout act\, drawing in crowds from around the
  world with their captivating live performances and exceptional musiciansh
 ip. They have performed at some of the most prestigious venues & festivals
  across the UK and Europe including Cambridge Folk Festival\, Bloom festiv
 al (Dublin)\, Montelago festival (Italy)\,Towersey Festival\, a headline s
 lot at Costa Festival Ibiza 2023\, Birmingham Symphony Hall\, The Union Ch
 apel\, Kings Place London along with regular tours of Scotland and Europe.
  \n\n\n\nRanagri are Dónal Rogers\, a prolific songwriter and producer\, 
 who has joined forces with the exceptional skills of renowned flautist Eli
 za Marshall\, harpist Eleanor Dunsdon and percussionist Jordan Murray. Tog
 ether\, Ranagri establish a fresh and modern sonic landscape within the fo
 lk genre\, captivating audiences both domestically and internationally\, a
 n energetic festival band yet equally at home with their more intimate wri
 ting and thought provoking lyrics. They are as happy to make you dance as 
 they are to make you smile or shed a tear\, passionately delving into curr
 ent world topics\, playing with politics\, and creating uplifting music to
  lyrics with great depth. \n\n\n\nAndrea Kirwin \n\n\n\nFor 20 years Austr
 alian/Fijian singer-songwriter Andrea Kirwin has been performing on the Au
 stralian Folk Festival scene and has built a career through her live shows
 \, her knack for storytelling and her love for her music community. Andrea
 ’s style is laid back\, giving space for her songs – and voice – to 
 really shine. Performing on Vocals\, Guitar\, Cigar box guitar and Stomp\,
  Andrea’s original songs are written in a range of genres including Folk
 \, Soul\, Blues and Roots and World music. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is co
 mmitted to an inclusive and safe experience for all. Gang Gang Cafe is whe
 elchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We have zero tolerance for h
 arassment and have support measures in place to ensure everyone’s safety
 . For specific accessibility needs or assistance\, please contact us in ad
 vance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang
  Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people\, the Traditional Cust
 odians of the land where our events take place. We pay our respects to the
 ir Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and recognise their enduring con
 nection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are grateful to celebrate 
 music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260227T024835Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/ranagri-england-at-gang-gang/
END:VEVENT
